# 16. AUTHENTICATION & ADMIN SECURITY

Use Firebase Authentication.

Create a secure initial admin account using the credentials supplied by the website owner during deployment.

IMPORTANT SECURITY REQUIREMENTS:

- Never hardcode the admin password in frontend code.
- Never expose credentials in public JavaScript bundles.
- Use secure server-side authentication.
- Use Firebase custom claims or another verified server-side role mechanism.
- Only authorized admins can access admin operations.
- Users must not be able to grant themselves admin privileges.
- Include password change and logout functionality.
- Protect admin routes and Firebase operations with security rules.
- Store privileged secrets in secure environment variables or managed secrets.
- Use password reset and recovery procedures.

The initial admin password should be changed if it has been reused elsewhere.

