Use subcollections for growing datasets such as messages and comments.

Do not store unbounded conversation history inside one Firestore document.

Use pagination, timestamps, appropriate indexes, and efficient queries.

## 17.1. Firebase Security Rules

- Public visitors can read published characters.
- Only admins can create, update, delete, publish, or hide characters.
- Only admins can manage music and announcements.
- Members can edit their own profiles.
- Members can only read conversations in which they participate.
- Members can only edit or delete their own permitted messages.
- Users cannot change their own admin role.
- Votes must be validated by trusted server-side functions.
- Validate uploaded file types and sizes.
- Never expose Firebase Admin SDK credentials.

